      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg a day, which is twice the usual maximum for oral ibuprofen in adults. The maximum is 3,200 mg a day under medical supervision, and 1,200 mg a day for over-the-counter use. At 6,400 mg a day, the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events is high, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Typical dosing:** 400\u2013800 mg by mouth three or four times daily, up to 3,200 mg a day. For example, 800 mg \u00d7 4 is 3,200 mg a day.\n- **Possible typo:** If the order was meant to be 600 mg or 800 mg per dose, or 1600 mg a day in total, please confirm.\n\nMedication orders should also come from a licensed prescriber who is treating the patient. If a clinician on the medicine service confirms the intended dose, I can enter it. I can also enter one of the standard regimens above if you tell me which one."
      }
